        "grounded": true,
        "answer": "Array.map can be used to create a new array by calling a function on every element of the original array. For example, if we have an array of squares, we can use map to convert it to a new array of circles. This is shown in the code where an array of objects is mapped to a new array of strings that only contain the user names [1].\n\nThe function passed to map is called on every element in the original array, and it's responsible for computing a new value and returning it. This is demonstrated in the example where the user names are mapped to a new array of strings [1].\n\nHere's an example of how this might look in code:\n```javascript\nconst users = [{ name: 'John' }, { name: 'Jane' }, { name: 'Bob' }];\nconst userNames = users.map(user => user.name);\n```\nThis would create a new array `userNames` containing the strings 'John', 'Jane', and 'Bob' [1].",
